#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186334322 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7ac34a18-053d-5eab-8c2c-bd0f15658186" :knowledge-point/title "Solving First-Order Linear ODEs Using Variation of Parameters"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "64c67d11-b747-58f1-9c45-0d2dc1ee9620" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334324} {:answer/id #uuid "55ba33df-887d-5ab1-9224-442eff8b598d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{-3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334325} {:answer/id #uuid "705de41f-728e-5e72-934f-784e9330c9c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{-7x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334326} {:answer/id #uuid "df762619-3c48-5190-818f-3d565f61a66b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{7x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334327} {:answer/id #uuid "9b1eb710-e113-550f-9af4-a57d73884daf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{-4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334328}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9b1eb710-e113-550f-9af4-a57d73884daf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{-4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334328} :answer-field/id #uuid "3473014a-7899-56f9-8c7f-3df389b43121" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334323} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e9e21c60-8d5b-5e78-9a2b-255094397902" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{4}{e}^{-4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334330} {:answer/id #uuid "ef288faf-a7bf-59b4-9230-f7e17523bf1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{4}{e}^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334331} {:answer/id #uuid "f31a5fe7-0444-593f-9b1c-f5b509cce7fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}{e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334332} {:answer/id #uuid "d957b655-cbda-5bb9-816a-3ba0d13244f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7{e}^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334333} {:answer/id #uuid "b05bd306-bced-5223-9a01-293a811c741a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334334}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ef288faf-a7bf-59b4-9230-f7e17523bf1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{4}{e}^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334331} :answer-field/id #uuid "f7526a33-2684-5209-ad31-0f90d2c2015d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334329} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "536fae60-901b-57bd-b475-e2ffcd9d57d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334336} {:answer/id #uuid "a396b4f0-425b-5695-972d-bbae38db063c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7{e}^{-4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334337} {:answer/id #uuid "da9a978a-6f04-5b0e-b1ba-330671ce800b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334338} {:answer/id #uuid "c7bc405d-b6cc-5e73-aaa6-f82a0eedb9b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{4}{e}^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334339} {:answer/id #uuid "f8a47ab9-58a1-5e66-98c1-7ec2dc3ab4ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334340}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "536fae60-901b-57bd-b475-e2ffcd9d57d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334336} :answer-field/id #uuid "70921230-38fa-5ad2-9101-f1bfc99a73de" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334335}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2c874b63-ba61-5224-951d-5ad10fbf990c" :question/math-academy-id "q-337375" :question/problem "Consider the first-order linear ODE\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4y=7.\n$$\n\nWe wish to solve this equation using the method of variation of parameters (VOP).\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n$\\,$ According to VOP, we assume a particular solution of the form {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Solving for $u,$ we have $u(x)=$ {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Therefore, the particular solution is ${y}_{p}(x)=$ {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation, we must find the sum of the complementary and particular solutions.\n\nTo find the complementary solution ${y}_{c},$ we solve the corresponding homogeneous equation, given by\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}^{′}+4{y}_{c}=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we find that the complementary solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A{e}^{-4x}\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nThe method of variation of parameters constructs a particular solution by varying the constant in the homogeneous solution. So, to find a suitable ${y}_{p},$ we set $A=u(x)$ in the complementary solution, as given by the following ansatz:\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=u(x){e}^{-4x}\n$$\n\nIntuitively, this form of ${y}_{p}$ tracks the homogeneous solution but with a varying amplitude.\n\nTo find $u,$ we substitute our ansatz into the equation, apply the product rule to the derivative term, and simplify to isolate ${u}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(u{e}^{-4x})}^{′}+4(u{e}^{-4x}) & =7 \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{-4x}-4u{e}^{-4x}+4u{e}^{-4x} & =7 \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{-4x}-\\cancel{4u{e}^{-4x}}+\\cancel{4u{e}^{-4x}} & =7 \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{-4x} & =7 \\\\ {u}^{′} & =7{e}^{4x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides with respect to $x$ (omitting the arbitrary constant), we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′} & =7{e}^{4x} \\\\ \\int {u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 7{e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ u & =\\frac{7}{4}{e}^{4x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${y}_{p}=u(x){e}^{-4x},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p} & =u(x){e}^{-4x} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{4}{e}^{4x}\\cdot {e}^{-4x} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186334341 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7ac34a18-053d-5eab-8c2c-bd0f15658186" :knowledge-point/title "Solving First-Order Linear ODEs Using Variation of Parameters"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "45b747e4-2547-559c-94e6-c31c4087f78e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{-2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334343} {:answer/id #uuid "9675e90c-04c4-575a-bb2c-e0e709f70828" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334344} {:answer/id #uuid "49ca8f81-e15c-50ed-a80f-2153a5ffdd94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334345} {:answer/id #uuid "e17900bb-7c78-53d4-9cb9-492d9e7ba0b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334346} {:answer/id #uuid "3fdac4b0-c9ab-5666-82c2-ce9a8b86ff2d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334347}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e17900bb-7c78-53d4-9cb9-492d9e7ba0b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334346} :answer-field/id #uuid "f3c6b39e-c0e6-5e97-b21d-45795ae718eb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334342} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "164457d8-f242-5667-8861-eee54e6415e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int {e}^{-x}(5-2x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334349} {:answer/id #uuid "da11807c-e743-5c27-8928-2e14f5fa3e26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int {e}^{-x}(2x-5)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334350} {:answer/id #uuid "f01d3319-75eb-5fca-84cb-9be41c1410fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int {e}^{-x}(2x+5)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334351} {:answer/id #uuid "4ae598fd-19c8-5a1f-9259-99ca2d19ee29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int {e}^{x}(2x-5)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334352}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "da11807c-e743-5c27-8928-2e14f5fa3e26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int {e}^{-x}(2x-5)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334350} :answer-field/id #uuid "55e62dcf-aa19-5497-ba40-81f81e3e1296" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334348} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40a21d53-dcfe-53dd-a728-83798bf9143e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{x}\\int {e}^{-x}(2x-5)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334354} {:answer/id #uuid "d8e8b798-d22f-50fd-bf1a-88ac5a6048a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{x}\\int {e}^{-x}(2x+5)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334355} {:answer/id #uuid "d896c2f3-75cc-50d4-970c-4eaca6a23ecd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-x}\\int {e}^{-x}(5-2x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334356} {:answer/id #uuid "1356ddff-33f8-5b55-9c44-d409f635827b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-x}\\int {e}^{x}(2x-5)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334357}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "40a21d53-dcfe-53dd-a728-83798bf9143e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{x}\\int {e}^{-x}(2x-5)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334354} :answer-field/id #uuid "924c0b44-0735-5ca2-86fa-9133546f1d78" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334353}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bc82baf7-6e13-5137-9b62-5ced3f36541b" :question/math-academy-id "q-337395" :question/problem "Consider the first-order linear ODE\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-y=2x-5.\n$$\n\nWe wish to solve this equation using the method of variation of parameters (VOP).\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n$\\,$ According to VOP, we assume a particular solution of the form {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Solving for $u,$ we have $u(x)=$ {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Therefore, the particular solution is ${y}_{p}(x)=$ {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation, we must find the sum of the complementary and particular solutions.\n\nTo find the complementary solution ${y}_{c},$ we solve the corresponding homogeneous equation, given by\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}^{′}-{y}_{c}=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we find that the complementary solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A{e}^{x}\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nThe method of variation of parameters constructs a particular solution by varying the constant in the homogeneous solution. So, to find a suitable ${y}_{p},$ we set $A=u(x)$ in the complementary solution, as given by the following ansatz:\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=u(x){e}^{x}\n$$\n\nIntuitively, this form of ${y}_{p}$ tracks the homogeneous solution but with a varying amplitude.\n\nTo find $u,$ we substitute our ansatz into the equation, apply the product rule to the derivative term, and simplify to isolate ${u}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(u{e}^{x})}^{′}-(u{e}^{x}) & =2x-5 \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{x}+u{e}^{x}-u{e}^{x} & =2x-5 \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{x}+\\cancel{u{e}^{x}}-\\cancel{u{e}^{x}} & =2x-5 \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{x} & =2x-5 \\\\ {u}^{′} & ={e}^{-x}(2x-5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides with respect to $x$ (omitting the arbitrary constant), we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′} & ={e}^{-x}(2x-5) \\\\ \\int {u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{-x}(2x-5)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ u & =\\int {e}^{-x}(2x-5)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${y}_{p}=u(x){e}^{x},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p} & =u(x){e}^{x} \\\\  & =\\int {e}^{-x}(2x-5)\\,\\text{d}x\\cdot {e}^{x} \\\\  & ={e}^{x}\\int {e}^{-x}(2x-5)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186334358 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5fb547a-2518-5db9-b1b1-aab8d80328af" :knowledge-point/title "Solving First-Order Linear ODEs Using VOP When the Forcing Term is Part of the Complementary Solution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d7bab9d3-a643-542a-91fd-0e987dea1805" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{-6x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334360} {:answer/id #uuid "e49089fe-9191-56bd-9fd3-d50a5325ad69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334361} {:answer/id #uuid "630b3248-5005-584a-9b13-09b251396ece" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{8x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334362} {:answer/id #uuid "0429c658-1f53-5839-9694-4745d2e0a383" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{6x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334363} {:answer/id #uuid "f5ca964f-b2ff-57f5-8da3-0c0f0c2fd6c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{-4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334364}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0429c658-1f53-5839-9694-4745d2e0a383" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{6x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334363} :answer-field/id #uuid "acdfc81d-1134-588e-b05a-9cfa412ea176" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334359} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e43bf03d-2317-58f5-a123-5e887ea00ccd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{6x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334366} {:answer/id #uuid "63c8d43b-2f41-58e0-9680-8fee97a8b7e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-6x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334367} {:answer/id #uuid "44941112-7960-5e1a-99c4-e7d00ffcef68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x{e}^{-6x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334368} {:answer/id #uuid "688f7cae-2b20-5c4c-b1e5-1cfccbce95f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334369} {:answer/id #uuid "4fcf68d5-d666-556c-89ec-e92ffae0f1cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334370} {:answer/id #uuid "65ca9102-a608-52bb-9c29-de9e89e0ce20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x{e}^{6x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334371}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4fcf68d5-d666-556c-89ec-e92ffae0f1cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334370} :answer-field/id #uuid "1bae32b5-209c-52db-8bf0-51f759703a16" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334365} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3477f2d9-8b83-59c5-94c2-ef9cab50edb9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{6x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334373} {:answer/id #uuid "68755ee1-9167-51c8-a3c1-da85854f9d77" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-6x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334374} {:answer/id #uuid "a2f9ca7a-6ce4-5928-a0ca-aea74f923bb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x{e}^{-6x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334375} {:answer/id #uuid "e3444fad-a327-55d0-bf94-492195ca781f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x{e}^{6x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334376}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e3444fad-a327-55d0-bf94-492195ca781f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x{e}^{6x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334376} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5e31c6b-2156-5254-9244-78abe674b418" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334372}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3500ae78-1cc6-5c2f-9a74-6462d1a0b3b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-337533" :question/problem "Consider the first-order linear ODE\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-6y={e}^{6x}.\n$$\n\nWe wish to solve this equation using the method of variation of parameters (VOP).\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n$\\,$ According to VOP, we assume a particular solution of the form {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Solving for $u,$ we have $u(x)=$ {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Therefore, the particular solution is ${y}_{p}(x)=$ {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation, we must find the sum of the complementary and particular solutions.\n\nTo find the complementary solution ${y}_{c},$ we solve the corresponding homogeneous equation, given by\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}^{′}-6{y}_{c}=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we find that the complementary solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A{e}^{6x}\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nThe method of variation of parameters constructs a particular solution by varying the constant in the homogeneous solution. So, to find a suitable ${y}_{p},$ we set $A=u(x)$ in the complementary solution, as given by the following ansatz:\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=u(x){e}^{6x}\n$$\n\nIntuitively, this form of ${y}_{p}$ tracks the homogeneous solution but with a varying amplitude.\n\nTo find $u,$ we substitute our ansatz into the equation, apply the product rule to the derivative term, and simplify to isolate ${u}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(u{e}^{6x})}^{′}-6(u{e}^{6x}) & ={e}^{6x} \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{6x}+6u{e}^{6x}-6u{e}^{6x} & ={e}^{6x} \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{6x}+\\cancel{6u{e}^{6x}}-\\cancel{6u{e}^{6x}} & ={e}^{6x} \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{6x} & ={e}^{6x} \\\\ {u}^{′} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides with respect to $x$ (omitting the arbitrary constant), we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′} & =1 \\\\ \\int {u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ u & =x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${y}_{p}=u(x){e}^{6x},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p} & =u(x){e}^{6x} \\\\  & =x{e}^{6x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186334377 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5fb547a-2518-5db9-b1b1-aab8d80328af" :knowledge-point/title "Solving First-Order Linear ODEs Using VOP When the Forcing Term is Part of the Complementary Solution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27d9c1bf-df94-5034-b7d5-c2fbdfa02570" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{-6x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334379} {:answer/id #uuid "67d3c8b4-ce61-543e-bd7e-390f22c306ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334380} {:answer/id #uuid "604c778f-b671-507e-a9d8-b3d0ac50bd1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{6x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334381} {:answer/id #uuid "9f3bc0e0-9b9f-5538-a731-166ad58fae0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{-3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334382} {:answer/id #uuid "61e78fa5-9bad-5b54-b1fc-09cae2231558" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{9x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334383}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "67d3c8b4-ce61-543e-bd7e-390f22c306ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334380} :answer-field/id #uuid "723d8a84-678e-5285-a684-be8ef3d5591a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334378} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ca0431f0-e143-510b-8cd5-319146412df7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-x{e}^{-6x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334385} {:answer/id #uuid "7764e3d6-6ee3-5bf5-ad1c-9b8bd7efaa8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\frac{1}{2}x{e}^{-6x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334386} {:answer/id #uuid "b15f99c4-88c6-5612-9cd8-15e372950f90" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-6x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334387} {:answer/id #uuid "cf0af68c-6217-5685-9f2f-f6c62da909c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x-{e}^{-6x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334388}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b15f99c4-88c6-5612-9cd8-15e372950f90" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-6x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334387} :answer-field/id #uuid "17747586-1c4a-5fca-9b10-92d4eb179043" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334384} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "137c9ba6-d2ba-5a39-b61c-af416817e6d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{3x}-x{e}^{-3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334390} {:answer/id #uuid "af238b7c-27f4-5751-ae7c-947df35f94ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x{e}^{3x}-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334391} {:answer/id #uuid "6b12a7f6-8a45-566d-b5dd-011fdfad4e79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{3x}-\\frac{1}{2}x{e}^{-3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334392} {:answer/id #uuid "3390a2ea-9386-5a81-9669-6ba5366dea4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x{e}^{3x}-{e}^{-3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334393}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "af238b7c-27f4-5751-ae7c-947df35f94ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x{e}^{3x}-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334391} :answer-field/id #uuid "29a9537d-e6fc-50e4-92c2-a5164921c0d4" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334389}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "30381914-6c05-5474-8e6f-cee39aeb98f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-338129" :question/problem "Consider the first-order linear ODE\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3y=6\\operatorname{cosh}⁡3x.\n$$\n\nWe wish to solve this equation using the method of variation of parameters (VOP).\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n$\\,$ According to VOP, we assume a particular solution of the form {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Solving for $u,$ we have $u(x)=$ {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Therefore, the particular solution is ${y}_{p}(x)=$ {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation, we must find the sum of the complementary and particular solutions.\n\nTo find the complementary solution ${y}_{c},$ we solve the corresponding homogeneous equation, given by\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}^{′}-3{y}_{c}=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we find that the complementary solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A{e}^{3x}\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nThe method of variation of parameters constructs a particular solution by varying the constant in the homogeneous solution. So, to find a suitable ${y}_{p},$ we set $A=u(x)$ in the complementary solution, as given by the following ansatz:\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=u(x){e}^{3x}\n$$\n\nIntuitively, this form of ${y}_{p}$ tracks the homogeneous solution but with a varying amplitude.\n\nTo find $u,$ we substitute our ansatz into the equation, apply the product rule to the derivative term, and simplify to isolate ${u}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(u{e}^{3x})}^{′}-3(u{e}^{3x}) & =6\\operatorname{cosh}⁡3x \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{3x}+3u{e}^{3x}-3u{e}^{3x} & =6\\operatorname{cosh}⁡3x \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{3x}+\\cancel{3u{e}^{3x}}-\\cancel{3u{e}^{3x}} & =6\\operatorname{cosh}⁡3x \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{3x} & =6\\operatorname{cosh}⁡3x \\\\ {u}^{′} & =6{e}^{-3x}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡3x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cosh}⁡3x=\\frac{{e}^{3x}+{e}^{-3x}}{2}\n$$\n\nour equation for $u$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′} & =6{e}^{-3x}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡3x \\\\  & =6{e}^{-3x}(\\frac{{e}^{3x}+{e}^{-3x}}{2}) \\\\  & =3{e}^{-3x}({e}^{3x}+{e}^{-3x}) \\\\  & =3+3{e}^{-6x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides with respect to $x$ (omitting the arbitrary constant), we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′} & =3+3{e}^{-6x} \\\\ \\int {u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 3+3{e}^{-6x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ u & =3x-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-6x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${y}_{p}=u(x){e}^{3x},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p} & =u(x){e}^{3x} \\\\  & =3x{e}^{3x}-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-3x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186334394 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7ac34a18-053d-5eab-8c2c-bd0f15658186" :knowledge-point/title "Solving First-Order Linear ODEs Using Variation of Parameters"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "93613f48-348c-5950-a6db-3fcaf4392705" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{-5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334396} {:answer/id #uuid "c65b486a-aca0-594c-aa78-acbb135c9c12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334397} {:answer/id #uuid "02a6cece-6b1c-5f98-a1a5-0b4926de0c5d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334398} {:answer/id #uuid "4644aa7a-c2b1-562b-956a-69255128e5ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334399} {:answer/id #uuid "5a281eaf-9838-521f-aeb1-7a4d3237e311" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334400}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "93613f48-348c-5950-a6db-3fcaf4392705" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{-5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334396} :answer-field/id #uuid "69cc0f77-6ac5-52f3-a40d-83ef2ee033ae" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334395} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d50b428-5904-53e9-aafc-63fe324ac2f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{-6x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334402} {:answer/id #uuid "88452c5f-8a58-59ca-a5e3-ea8f945011ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334403} {:answer/id #uuid "4ff0d87a-791d-56d6-a35b-13ea0c1c560c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334404} {:answer/id #uuid "a8b72283-bd03-5823-8fc8-c3187c5234ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334405} {:answer/id #uuid "2bdb4523-95c3-5a1f-80ac-392720ea1d1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334406}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "88452c5f-8a58-59ca-a5e3-ea8f945011ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334403} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ff1666d-8206-58c7-8ac5-da234dc132b4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334401} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "038a9f85-7961-5df4-ba32-d00e2a387840" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}{e}^{-5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334408} {:answer/id #uuid "f7ceeae0-c237-5a45-bdd1-a02af30abc38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{9x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334409} {:answer/id #uuid "8b0a8034-0050-5ad8-9e55-735371a45d6d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334410} {:answer/id #uuid "6ce223a7-b6f4-5df0-898a-5ccae4556d60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334411} {:answer/id #uuid "9c17370a-28ae-503e-8962-d80b555d81ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334412}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6ce223a7-b6f4-5df0-898a-5ccae4556d60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334411} :answer-field/id #uuid "d1f65fd1-cf0a-5578-b6d0-c23d9faa2fa1" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334407}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3b0212f2-f2fb-5e50-b8a7-448c254b9133" :question/math-academy-id "q-352892" :question/problem "Consider the first-order linear ODE\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+5y=2{e}^{-x}.\n$$\n\nWe wish to solve this equation using the method of variation of parameters (VOP).\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n$\\,$ According to VOP, we assume a particular solution of the form {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Solving for $u,$ we have $u(x)=$ {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Therefore, the particular solution is ${y}_{p}(x)=$ {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation, we must find the sum of the complementary and particular solutions.\n\nTo find the complementary solution ${y}_{c},$ we solve the corresponding homogeneous equation, given by\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}^{′}+5{y}_{c}=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we find that the complementary solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A{e}^{-5x}\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nThe method of variation of parameters constructs a particular solution by varying the constant in the homogeneous solution. So, to find a suitable ${y}_{p},$ we set $A=u(x)$ in the complementary solution, as given by the following ansatz:\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=u(x){e}^{-5x}\n$$\n\nIntuitively, this form of ${y}_{p}$ tracks the homogeneous solution but with a varying amplitude.\n\nTo find $u,$ we substitute our ansatz into the equation, apply the product rule to the derivative term, and simplify to isolate ${u}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(u{e}^{-5x})}^{′}+5(u{e}^{-5x}) & =2{e}^{-x} \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{-5x}-5u{e}^{-5x}+5u{e}^{-5x} & =2{e}^{-x} \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{-5x}-\\cancel{5u{e}^{-5x}}+\\cancel{5u{e}^{-5x}} & =2{e}^{-x} \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{-5x} & =2{e}^{-x} \\\\ {u}^{′} & =2{e}^{4x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides with respect to $x$ (omitting the arbitrary constant), we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′} & =2{e}^{4x} \\\\ \\int {u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 2{e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ u & =\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{4x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${y}_{p}=u(x){e}^{-5x},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p} & =u(x){e}^{-5x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{4x}\\cdot {e}^{-5x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
